{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "label": "Snapshots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A periodic dump of current state so recovery loads the latest snapshot and replays only events after it. The trade-off is disk space and write throughput for bounded recovery time; the framework never auto-snapshots."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicyhook", "label": "snapshotPolicy() / SnapshotPolicy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Configuring a snapshot policy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(seqNr, state, event) => boolean, called after every event apply. Defaults to () => false, so no policy means no snapshots."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore", "label": "SnapshotStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Where snapshots live", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The pluggable store, wired at system creation via withPersistence and independent of the journal - Cassandra journal plus object-storage snapshots is a valid mix. It returns the latest snapshot for a persistenceId on recovery; older ones need the lower-level API."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotintervalchoice", "label": "Picking the snapshot interval", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Picking the snapshot interval", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three numbers move against each other: recovery time (lower N is faster), snapshot write cost (every snapshot serializes the full state, so higher N amortizes it), and storage. everyNEvents(100) is a reasonable starting point - measure recovery latency in production before changing it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_retentionbesteffort", "label": "Retention is best-effort; the write is not", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Retention is best-effort; the write is not", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Once the snapshot is durable, save resolves and a failed keepN prune is swallowed. The two halves have opposite failure meanings: a failed write means your snapshot does not exist and retrying is right, while a failed prune means one harmless extra row loadLatest cannot see. Reporting the second as the first would tell a caller to retry a write that already succeeded, and an actor treating snapshot failure as fatal would die over housekeeping."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_recoveryflowwithsnapshots", "label": "Recovery flow with snapshots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Recovery flow with snapshots", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preStart loads the latest snapshot (or falls back to initialState at seq 0), reads events from seq+1 and folds them; onEvent stays pure either way - the snapshot is just where replay starts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotadapter", "label": "SnapshotAdapter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Snapshot adapters - schema evolution", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Upcasts old snapshots on load when the state shape changes; with one set, snapshots are persisted in a { _v, _t, _e } envelope. The alternative is deleting old snapshots and replaying from the still-current event log."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_adaptersmustmatch", "label": "Snapshot adapters must match the event adapter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Common pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Events with an adapter but snapshots without means recovery loads a V1 snapshot and applies V2 events to it - wrong shape, silently broken state. Either both have adapters or neither does."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshoteveryeventantipattern", "label": "Snapshotting after every event", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Common pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every persist would also write the full state, doubling or tripling write cost for non-trivial states. If that is the behavior you want, DurableStateActor is the shape designed for 'always current'."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicyhook", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotintervalchoice", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_retentionbesteffort", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_recoveryflowwithsnapshots", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotadapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_adaptersmustmatch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshoteveryeventantipattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_adaptersmustmatch", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_eventadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Common pitfalls", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshots", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotpolicyhook", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Configuring a snapshot policy", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshot_stores_in_memory_inmemorysnapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Where snapshots live", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshot_stores_sqlite_sqlitesnapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/snapshots.mdx", "source_location": "## Where snapshots live", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_snapshotstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshot_stores_cassandra_cassandrasnapshotstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confi